shape theory.uniqueness : theory.minimal {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 4.6 (Uniqueness).
// There is exactly one minimal shape. Not one "up to structural
// equivalence," but one.
//
// Suppose two minimal shapes exist. Both have no distinguishing
// character beyond self-reference. Both have identical structure.
// To be two distinct shapes, something must distinguish them.
// But both have identical structure (minimal), identical character
// (none), and identical reference (self only). In persistence
// structure, identity is structural: two things are the same thing
// if and only if they have the same structure and the same character
// trajectory. Therefore they are identical.
//
// Derives from: theory.minimal
  """
}
